  "why": "PA3 in-house migration: Paper A's 'representation-dependence' paragraph cited a chemprop v2 scorer.  The project red line requires the predictive line to be backed by the self-developed D-MPNN.  This artifact re-measures the same cross-metal LOMO column with the in-house MetalAwareDMPNN (metal_injection='none', zero-shot) on the same 24 h probe cohort and the same ligand-disjoint LOMO split.",
  "caveats": [
    "Capacity is NOT matched: chemprop v2 used d_h=300 depth=3, the in-house D-MPNN uses hidden=128 depth=3.  Differences here are reported as a scorer/representation comparison, not a like-for-like capacity comparison.",
    "Per-metal test folds are small for Rh (n=51), Os (n=36) and Re (n=74).  The label-permutation null on the fixed seed-42 ranking is the reference (1,000 shuffles); at those sizes the null sd is ~0.09-0.11, so a nominal 0.5 is not the right line.",
    "Only the CROSS column is seed-42 for the permutation null and the bootstrap CI; the reported cross AUCs are 5-seed means.  The CI's observed_auc is the seed-42 ranking, so it sits inside the seed spread around the 5-seed mean.",
    "The within-metal column is carried from the committed 24 h artifact (epochs=30, 5 split seeds); the cross column is epochs=50.  The two columns are not the same training budget — the same asymmetry exists in the chemprop reference, where within and cross are separate runs."
  ],
